From caea6c15022a6a91ea1e7bdb3f06fe41b42f8863 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Diller <dillera@dillernet.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:23:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add a FujiNet-served DCD (HD20) chain on the external drive
 port

The drive side of the Directly Connected Disk protocol, bit-timed through
the IWM like a real device: phase states 0-7, !HSHK on the sense line,
7-to-8 group coding with holdoff/resume, CA3 (LSTRB) daisy chaining, and
read/write/status/ID/format commands. Blocks come from a FujiNet over TCP
using the FujiNet Mac board's Pico <-> FujiNet protocol, so the emulated
Mac talks to fujinet-nio exactly as a real Mac does through the board.

Enabled with SNOW_FUJINET_DCD=host:port. Units come and go as the FujiNet
reports mounts; save states skip the live link.

Also adds testrunner/fnrun, a scripted headless runner (mouse, keys,
screenshots) used to test it.
